First, we will prepare our disk for installation. At least two partitions are
required to be present on the disk:
    - an EFI system partition
    - a root partition

If either of these does not exist, you can create them interactively by
following this step.

A general note on using this script:
If you abort the installation process at any time, you can restart at a specific
step by passing its number to the script as an argument, for example:
%1 4
Instead of the step's number you may also enter an alias for the step which
roughly describes its functionality and may be easier to remember. For example,
this is equivalent to the above command:
%1 mount

The alias is given at the beginning of each step. A list of number, aliases and
their corresponding steps may also be found in the readme.